From 5ffc8b2b192826df47f2f52b89e54bfc69ae3d03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:31:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 139/140] feat(gestures): make swipe action zones configurable

Release disabled swipe zones before consuming horizontal movement so None no longer blocks tab navigation. Claim only the enabled inward action for each physical edge, respect already-consumed gestures, and keep captured drags within their selected direction.

Add independent left and right swipe-zone width preferences with a 25% default and a 1-50% range. Apply the saved widths through the shared video, folder, and music-row swipe surface, with disjoint boundaries and live updates.

Add percentage sliders and proportional zone previews to the existing swipe settings page. Show 0% for None while preserving the configured width for re-enabling. Retain physical edge placement in RTL layouts, existing haptic behavior, and accessible slider labels.

Translate both new labels across all ten resource sets and expand settings-search keywords for zone width and percentage. The new preferences participate in the existing settings backup flow.

Validation: focused static source and API inspection, editor diagnostics, XML parsing and placeholder checks across all locales, and git diff --check. No builds, tests, formatters, or device validation were run under the static-only constraint.
